        "PMC8249401::web::029::influence_of_twin_boundary_distance"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Interphase and twin boundaries impede dislocation motion under sustained loading.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6045582::web::004::the_promise_of_dual_phase_high_entropy_a",
        "PMC8249401::web::029::influence_of_twin_boundary_distance"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed starting coating contains both FCC and BCC regions and a network of interphase boundaries.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6045582::web::004::the_promise_of_dual_phase_high_entropy_a"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The FCC regions in the proposed coating have the potential to form deformation twins.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6045582::web::004::the_promise_of_dual_phase_high_entropy_a",
        "PMC6045582::web::005::the_promise_of_dual_phase_high_entropy_a"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Changing deposition conditions and cooling rates can intentionally vary the density and continuity of interphase and twin boundaries.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Moderate-to-high-temperature sustained loading can produce creep governed by dislocation-based plasticity in the proposed coating.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11203300::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "FCC/BCC interphase boundaries act as obstacles to dislocation glide.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6045582::web::004::the_promise_of_dual_phase_high_entropy_a"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "FCC/BCC interphase boundaries promote twin-boundary nucleation and migration.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Twin-boundary migration can control plastic deformation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8249401::web::029::influence_of_twin_boundary_distance"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The combined interphase- and twin-boundary effect redistributes local stresses.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6045582::web::004::the_promise_of_dual_phase_high_entropy_a"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The combined boundary effect retards plastic flow and lowers the steady-state creep rate.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A coating with a high density of interphase and twin boundaries will have a lower steady-state creep rate than a coating with fewer such boundaries.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A coating with a high density of interphase and twin boundaries will exhibit greater work hardening than the baseline.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
